.TH STACKGAUGE 1 "2025" "stackgauge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stackgauge \- static stack depth analysis for embedded firmware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stackgauge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIMAP_FILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stackgauge
parses linker map files and GCC
.I .su
stack-usage files to report per-function frame sizes and, where call-graph
data is available, worst-case cumulative stack depth.
.PP
Designed to run as a pre-commit hook so stack overflows are caught before
they reach hardware.
.PP
Supported toolchains: GCC + GNU ld, ARM/Keil MDK (armlink), and
ESP-IDF (Xtensa/GCC). The map format is auto-detected unless overridden
with
.BR \-\-toolchain .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I MAP_FILE
Linker map file to analyse.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-su\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Search
.I DIR
recursively for
.I .su
files. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-su\-file \fIFILE\fR
Add a single
.I .su
file explicitly. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-cgraph\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Search
.I DIR
recursively for
.I *.cgraph
dumps. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-cgraph\-file \fIFILE\fR
Add a single
.I .cgraph
file explicitly. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-dir \fINAME\fR
Skip directories named
.I NAME
during
.I .su
/
.I .cgraph
search. Repeatable. CompilerIdC, CompilerIdCXX, and CompilerIdASM are
excluded by default.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-stack\-threshold " " \fIN\fR
Fail (exit 1) if worst-case stack exceeds
.I N
bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-depth\-threshold \fIN\fR
Fail (exit 1) if call depth exceeds
.I N
(ARM/Keil or GNU ld + cgraph).
.TP
.B \-\-top\-n \fIN\fR
Number of functions to show in the report (default: 10). See also
.BR \-v .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show all functions, not just the top N.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
Output format:
.B text
(default) or
.BR json .
.TP
.B \-\-toolchain \fIname\fR
Force map format:
.BR gnu\-ld " | " arm\-keil " | " esp\-idf .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Config file (default:
.IR stackgauge.toml ).
CLI flags always override config values.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All thresholds passed (or no thresholds set).
.TP
.B 1
A stack or depth threshold was exceeded.
.TP
.B 2
Fatal error (missing file, parse failure, etc.).
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
Place a
.I stackgauge.toml
in your project root or pass
.B \-c
to specify a path. CLI flags take precedence over config values.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
stack_threshold = 2048
depth_threshold = 12
top_n = 20
su_dirs = ["build/CMakeFiles", "build"]
# toolchain = "gnu-ld"
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Report top-10 largest frames (GNU ld):
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/
.TP
With worst-case depth analysis:
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/ --cgraph-dir build/
.TP
Fail if stack > 2 KB or depth > 12:
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/ --stack-threshold 2048 --depth-threshold 12
.TP
JSON output:
.B stackgauge firmware.map --su-dir build/ --format json | jq .call_graph
.TP
ARM/Keil (call graph is embedded in the map):
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map
.SH PRE-COMMIT INTEGRATION
Add to
.I .pre-commit-config.yaml:
.PP
.nf
repos:
  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: stackgauge
        name: Stack depth analysis
        language: system
        entry: stackgauge
        args: [build/firmware.map, --su-dir=build/]
        pass_filenames: false
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gcc (1),
.BR ld (1)
